# Mathematical vocabulary: analysis, algebra, probability, optimization, geometry.
#
# Source for the 'math' entry in 'spelllang' (see the spell section of
# dotfiles/nvim/init.lua). One word per line; lines starting with # are comments.
# nvim never reads this file directly -- init.lua recompiles it with :mkspell
# into stdpath('data')/site/spell/math.utf-8.spl whenever this file is newer, so
# just edit, save, and restart nvim.
#
# Every word here was checked against nvim's bundled en dictionary and kept only
# because that dictionary lacks it -- so do not add words en already knows
# (matrix, manifold, eigenvalue, covariate, refactoring, ... are all fine
# already). Prefer lowercase: a lowercase entry also accepts the Capitalized and
# ALL-CAPS forms, while a capitalised entry only accepts itself. Hyphenated
# terms need no entry -- vim spell-checks each side separately, so "well-posed"
# and "zero-shot" already pass.
#
# Words you add with zg do NOT come here; they go to spell/en.utf-8.add.

